// Ch10 B06 "The causeway" (C, 2.5 min). R01: Reedhollow at the fen's heart, the Kirru watching from the
// platforms; they heard the Drowner fall. R02: Owa, the eldest who still swims (grey muzzle, white crest;
// ADR 0204 §4), looks at each human, long and plain. At KERRID her crest lifts a little, as Pell's did on
// the Corrow road (Kirru can smell anchored motes). She says NOTHING to him or of him: the beat is a look,
// the same length as her look at the others; only the crest differs (rule 4). R03: "Not you." Pell steps
// back off the causeway onto the last root and stands. Kerrid stays outside too, unasked, on the root
// beside Pell, facing the water. Nobody comments.
title: ch10_causeway
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
@letterbox on
@camera R01
@music reedhollow fade=1.0
@wait 3.0
@camera R02
@mark owa causeway_gate walk
@wait 1.5
@anim owa look_at toma
@wait 1.0
@anim owa look_at asha
@wait 1.0
@anim owa look_at rhen
@wait 1.0
@anim owa look_at kerrid
@anim owa crest_lift
@wait 1.0
@anim owa look_at asha
Owa as "The eldest" [neutral]: You cut the roots. The three are lifted. Come in. #line:ch10_causeway_001
@wait 1.0
@camera R03
@anim owa look_at pell
@wait 2.0
Owa as "The eldest" [cold]: Not you. #line:ch10_causeway_002
@mark pell causeway_last_root walk
@wait 1.5
Asha [tender]: He brought us here. He walked behind us the whole way. #line:ch10_causeway_003
Owa as "The eldest" [neutral]: Yes. Behind. He is good at standing behind. #line:ch10_causeway_004 #tn:"Literal, not sarcastic: the Kirru speak the human tongue without idioms."
@mark owa ring_owa walk
@wait 1.0
@mark kerrid causeway_last_root_b walk
@anim kerrid look_at water
@wait 2.0
<<set $ch10_pell_kept_out = true>>
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
